MPS CSA Desktop Application
===========================

The launch files in this folder start the Community Service Awards desktop app.

QUICK SETUP
-----------
Use "Setup CSA.command" on macOS or "Setup CSA.bat" on Windows. The setup
file checks for Python 3, installs it through Homebrew or Windows Package
Manager when available, creates the project virtual environment, and installs
all requirements. It is safe to run again.

MACOS
-----
1. Double-click "Setup CSA.command" in this run folder. If Homebrew is
   available, it installs Python automatically when Python is missing.
2. If Homebrew is not installed, install Python 3.9 or newer from
   https://www.python.org/downloads/ and run the setup file again.
3. To run setup manually, open Terminal and go to the project folder:

   cd /path/to/CSA

4. Create the virtual environment if setup was not used:

   python3 -m venv .venv

5. Install the application requirements if setup was not used:

   .venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

6. Double-click "Launch CSA.command" in this run folder.
   You may need to right-click it and choose Open the first time.

WINDOWS
-------
1. Double-click "Setup CSA.bat" in this run folder. If Windows Package
   Manager (winget) is available, it installs Python automatically when
   Python is missing.
2. If winget is unavailable, install Python 3.9 or newer from
   https://www.python.org/downloads/ with "Add Python to PATH" enabled, then
   run the setup file again.
3. To run setup manually, open Command Prompt and go to the project folder:

   cd C:\path\to\CSA

4. Create the virtual environment if setup was not used:

   py -m venv .venv

5. Install the application requirements if setup was not used:

   .venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt

6. Double-click "Launch CSA.bat" in this run folder.

DATA
----
The SQLite database is created in the project root as csa_database.db.
CSV templates and sample files are in the project's data folder.
Do not delete csa_database.db unless you intend to remove the stored data.

The launcher files are in this folder, while the Python application files remain
in the parent project folder. The launchers automatically change to that parent
folder before starting the application.
